## Context

Found by `worktree-gc` during `/lair` housekeeping (2026-09-04): two
worktrees skipped GC for uncommitted changes, both post-dating their
ticket's own close. Preserved as WIP commits, not discarded, per molt's
orphaned-WIP rule — content not reviewed, may be stale or superseded.

## Actions

1. `t556-v2-content-schema` (commit `b0969e4`): re-opens ticket 0556 (closed
   via PR #160) and edits 0554/0565. Review whether this is real leftover
   work or a stale/confused branch — the un-close in particular needs a
   human read before trusting it. Also carries a stray vitest cache file
   (`node_modules/.vite/...`) that contradicts its own `.gitignore` edit —
   clean that up regardless of the rest.
2. `t0583-zotero-6012-adapter` (commit `778478a`): a modified acceptance
   artifact and a new `bench/r10_host_baseline.py` script, after ticket 0583
   closed via PR #239. Likely legitimate follow-up measurement — review and
   either land it (new PR) or fold findings into a fresh ticket.

## Exit criteria
- Both branches reviewed; each either lands via its own PR or is explicitly
  dropped with a reason recorded here.
